    "text": {
     "en": "Meena walks to a stream near the bamboo bridge and floats a paper boat. She is delighted and makes many more.\nA naughty boy starts pushing and overturning her boats. Meena is angry and shouts Stop.\nHe says he did it for fun, but he agrees to stop. He asks Meena to help him play too.\nHe does not know how to fold a boat. Meena says it is easy and teaches him with coloured paper.\nThey float their boats together, and the story ends happily.\nThe story teaches us to solve problems kindly. Meena turned an angry moment into a new friend.\nNew words: stream, swiftly, delighted, overturning."
    }
